== 1. registered / unregistered ==
  ok    program key = sha1 of the program members in MEMBER ORDER (03 then 04, not zip order)
  ok    a registered image resolves: 'MYSET'
  ok    an unregistered image: exit 2, UNREGISTERED on stderr naming the registry, the program key on stdout
  ok    a missing image is named
== 1b. THE DUAL KEY ==
  ok    a non-program delta: SAME program key, DIFFERENT whole-set key
  ok    whole-set key resolves, and silently
  ok    program key resolves and ANNOUNCES itself on stderr
  ok    whole-set key WINS when both are present
CONTROL FIRED: wholeset-only-row — the twin (same program key, other whole-set key) got exit 2 against a whole-set-only registry
  ok    a whole-set-ONLY row is unreachable by the program fallback from the twin
  ok    the whole-set key does not move with the search-path chain
== 1c. --full: the resolved chain and the region rules ==
  ok    --full IS chain-dependent (folds in the parent set along the path) — which is why it is not the dispatch key
  ok    …and names the images it resolved
  ok    the lineage's region rules: prg 2 / key 1 / gfx-qsnd 1 (a .13m is not program: the regex excludes 'm')
== 2. [fingerprint] config: the program regex and the region rules are the consumer's ==
  ok    under the lineage's regex a fake image has no program members (refused)
  ok    a consumer regex selects fake.01+fake.02 as the program, in order
  ok    the config's registry and default_set are used (no --set, no --registry)
  ok    …and BBX_CONFIG selects the same config
  ok    --full uses the consumer's region rules
== 3. the other kinds ==
